---
code: lint-tool-absent
when-fires: a configured external linter is not on PATH, so its checks did not run. lint/source_external.rs. `{tool}` is the tool name.
why: 27R §4 dir-absent-is-info - a missing tool is the admin's environment, disclosed rather than silently skipped; --require-tools raises it to a hard CI error. World-as-payload: an honest trigger would have to run a real foreign tool, which replay never does.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- lint-tool-absent && mise run loom:promote -- lint-tool-absent`. `mise run loom:vars -- --all lint-tool-absent` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh
note[lint-tool-absent]: sm `shellcheck` was not found on PATH -- its checks were
skipped. Install it, pass --no-tools to silence this, or --require-tools to make
it a hard CI error.
